pair D = (10*sqrt(3),0);
label("$D$",D,S);
draw(B--D);
draw(rightanglemark(B,D,A,40));
[/asy]

From 30-60-90 triangle $ABD$, we have $BD = AB/2 = 10$.  From 45-45-90 triangle $BCD$, we have $BC = BD\sqrt{2} = \boxed{10\sqrt{2}}$. </think>
<answer> 10\sqrt{2} </answer>

