solution:
First, we rearrange the product as \[\left(\frac{123}{321}\right)\left(\frac{123}{321}\right)^{-1}
\left(\frac{456}{654}\right) \left(\frac{456}{654}\right)^{-1}\left(\frac{789}{987}\right)\left(\frac{789}{987}\right)^{-1}.\]Recall that $a^{-1}$ means the reciprocal of $a$. So $\left(\frac{123}{321}\right)\left(\frac{123}{321}\right)^{-1}$ is the fraction 123/321 times its reciprocal. By the definition of reciprocal, this product is 1. Similarly, $\left(\frac{456}{654}\right) \left(\frac{456}{654}\right)^{-1}$ and $\left(\frac{789}{987}\right)\left(\frac{789}{987}\right)^{-1}$ also equal 1. Therefore, the desired product is $1\cdot1\cdot 1=\boxed{1}$. </think>
